+
+
+`snapshot` is the complete, bounded VFS inventory used by reset evidence. Its
+request is:
+
+```json
+{"op":"snapshot","path":"/work","limits":{"max_entries":10000,"max_file_bytes":67108864,"max_response_bytes":4194304}}
+```
+
+The root must be a directory and cannot be a final symlink. The response records
+every raw VFS node below it in lexical order, including `.`. Directory, regular
+file, and symlink entries carry the canonical relative path and mode. Regular
+files additionally carry byte size and SHA-256; symlinks carry their raw target
+without traversal. The operation reads the VFS `NodeKind::File` byte slice
+directly, so it is not subject to the 16 MiB `read` transport cap. It rejects
+entry, aggregate-file-byte, or response bounds rather than omitting nodes.
+
+`snapshot_sha256` is SHA-256 of the compact UTF-8 JSON serialization of the
+`snapshot` object itself, whose fields are ordered `schema_version`, `root`,
+`limits`, and `entries`; entry fields are ordered `path`, `kind`, `mode`, `size`,
+`sha256`, `target`, with absent properties represented by JSON `null`.
